# Deterministic line endings across the fleet.
#
# Without this, the mother checked out CRLF (core.autocrlf=true) while the forks sat
# LF on disk, because fanouts write blob content directly and git does not rewrite an
# already-matching file. The consequence was a real trap: a working-tree comparison
# between mother and fork reported drift on EVERY sync-unit file, and a naive `cp`
# during a fanout would have rewritten line endings across the whole sync unit.
#
# eol=lf makes the working tree match the blob everywhere, so parity can be checked
# with a plain diff and the "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings stop.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.pdf binary
